+## 4. Credentials
+
+- **`PRIVATE_DATA_TOKEN`**: fine-grained token, only `stock-2-private-data`, Contents read/write. Needed by the 5 writers and by the check.
+- **`PRIVATE_DATA_READ`** (optional, recommended): the same with Contents **read-only**. With it, the 61 lab and reader workflows cannot change the owner's files even if a lab has a bug.
+- **How the token stays hidden:**
+  - it is passed to git through environment settings, never in a URL, a file, a commit, a log line or Telegram (tested);
+  - GitHub masks secrets in logs;
+  - fork pull requests never receive secrets.
+
+## 5. Tests (`test/private-data.test.mjs`, 28 tests; full suite 1,133 pass)
+
+**Before the cutover nothing in production changes:**
+- pull, push and show do nothing, even with the private repository reachable;
+- mirror waits for the check, then copies each change once;
+- verify is read-only.
+
+**Telegram commands, end to end** (the real `scan.mjs` with a local Telegram stub):
+- `bought WST 100.50 9`, `halal ZQC yes`, `sold WST 110 9` and `halal ZQC no` all reach the private repository;
+- the share count reaches it encrypted;
+- the halal file keeps its 1-space indent;
+- a stale local copy does not matter, because each round reads first.
+
+**Nightly scan save:**
+- the bot's newer stop is kept, as is the scan's change to another stock;
+- both sides' log lines are kept;
+- the practice account is saved.
+
+**Concurrency:** two jobs saving at the same moment both succeed, and neither change is lost.
+
+**Failures:**
+- an unreachable private repository stops the job before anything runs, with `data/` untouched;
+- no holdings file stops the job;
+- a failed save gives a non-zero exit and an error line;
+- a missing token after the cutover stops the job.
+
+**Mirror after the cutover** never runs, so a stale public copy cannot overwrite the private one.
+
+**Cutover:**
+- private files stop being tracked;
+- a later `git add data` cannot publish them;
+- verify passes, and flags a file that gets tracked again.
+
+**Rollback** restores every file exactly, tracks them again, and removes the mode file and the ignore block without losing other `.gitignore` lines.
+
+**Derived files:**
+- `signals.json` readers get the same `posVerdict`;
+- the SEC danger-filing SELL reason gives the same verdict from the private file;
+- the scrub moves the owner marks and leaves frozen verdicts untouched.
+
+**Publishing:**
+- the website publishes `index.html` only;
+- no workflow uploads a private file or the data folder as an artifact (artifacts are run logs).
+
+**Mutation check:** breaking the save step makes 4 tests fail, and breaking the mode guard makes 9 fail. The tests are not vacuous.
+
+## 6. Website and artifacts
+
+- **Pages source** is "GitHub Actions". `pages.yml` copies `index.html` only, and fails the run if anything else is in the site folder.
+- **Artifacts** are the lab run logs (`run.log` and similar). They contain counts, not holdings, and a test guards that no private file or folder is uploaded.
+- **Logs:**
+  - The bot's `run.log` stays on the runner.
+  - The squad 29 log line no longer names held stocks.
+
+## 7. Token renewal (the current token expires 2026-11-29 21:00 UTC)
+
+From the cutover on, every job stops when the token expires, so renew it before then. The daily verify (7:17 Kuwait) sends **"TOKEN EXPIRES IN N DAYS"** from 14 days ahead.
+
+Zero-downtime steps (about 22 Nov):
+
+1. GitHub → photo → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → **Fine-grained tokens** → **Generate new token**. Use the same settings as before (only `stock-2-private-data`; Contents: Read and write). Choose the longest expiry you are comfortable with.
+2. `drrazaq/Stock-2` → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → `PRIVATE_DATA_TOKEN` → **Update** → paste the new value.
+3. Actions → **Private data connection check** → Run workflow → action `verify`. Telegram reports PASSED with the new expiry date.
+4. **The next day,** delete the old token in Fine-grained tokens. Runs that started before step 2 still use it, for up to 6 hours.
+
+The same steps apply to `PRIVATE_DATA_READ`.
+
+## 8. Final cutover checklist
+
+| # | Check | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Connection check passed (read, write, read-back identical, repository private) | ✅ 28 Oct 09:37 UTC |
+| 2 | Every private file listed, including the 4 derived ones | ✅ 19 files |
+| 3 | `bought` / `sold` / `halal` reach the private repository (end-to-end test) | ✅ tested locally |
+| 4 | Nightly scan save keeps the bot's newer changes (test) | ✅ |
+| 5 | Concurrency, failure and rollback tests | ✅ |
+| 6 | Pages publishes `index.html` only; no artifact carries a private file | ✅ |
+| 7 | Mirror live in production for 2+ days: daily verify reports "N of N identical" | ⏳ starts with the first bot run on the new workflow (today about 12:15 UTC) |
+| 8 | Optional read-only token `PRIVATE_DATA_READ` added | ⏳ owner |
+| 9 | Token renewed or renewal planned before 29 Nov | ⏳ owner |
+| 10 | Owner approval, then a weekend run of the cutover (action `cutover`, confirm `CUTOVER`) | ⏳ owner |
+
+**What the cutover run does,** stopping before anything changes if a step fails:
+1. Stops the bot, scan, watcher and news runs.
+2. Moves the owner marks out of the 4 public files.
+3. Copies everything to the private repository and checks that it reads back identical.
+4. Stops tracking the 19 files (they remain in history) and adds them to `.gitignore`.
+5. Commits, verifies and restarts the bot.
+6. Reports on Telegram.
+
+## 9. Risks
+
+1. **Token expiry or a GitHub problem stops every job** after the cutover. This is by design: no job runs without the holdings. Mitigated by the 14-day warning and RUN FAILED messages.
+2. **A reader not detected** (a script reading a private file by a path the scan missed) would see no file after the cutover. 66 workflows were found from the scripts and their imports, and a test fails if a new one appears without a pull step.
+3. **Runs in flight at the cutover:** the cutover cancels the bot, scan, watcher and news runs. Run it on a weekend so the live watcher and the scan are not needed.
+4. **After the cutover, the owner edits these files only through the bot** (or in the private repository), not in the public one.
+5. **History remains public** (section 10).
+6. **Rollback re-publishes** the owner's files in the public repository.
+7. **Cost:** none. Actions stay in the public repository (free), and the private repository is a few hundred KB. Each job gains about 2–5 seconds.
+
+## 10. Historical exposure: what can and cannot be removed
+
+- **Git history.** Every past version of these files is in the public history (the bot commits every few minutes).
+  - **What can be done:** `git filter-repo` removes those paths from all history, followed by a force-push. All commit IDs change, every workflow must be paused, and clones break.
+  - **What it cannot fix:** GitHub keeps old commits reachable by ID until GitHub Support runs a cleanup on request, and copies already taken cannot be recalled. The repository had 0 forks on 28 Oct.
+- **Website deployments:** only the current one is served, and it is `index.html` only. Archive sites may hold old snapshots; removal requests go to them.
+- **Actions logs:** public for 90 days; they contain counts, not holdings. They can be deleted per run.
+- **Recommendation:** first the cutover (no new exposure), then decide on history.
+
+## 11. Unchanged
+
+- Trading rules, halal gate and marks, holdings, the frozen ranking experiment (A/B/C/D/R/R0) and live alert selection.
+- The squad 29 and hold-lab frozen verdicts (only the owner part of their output moved).
 
 ## Rollback
 
-- Stage 1: delete the secret `PRIVATE_DATA_TOKEN` and everything stops (no-op). The commit that added stage 1 can be reverted safely.
-- Stage 0: Settings → Pages → Source → "Deploy from a branch". This would publish the whole repository again, so it is not advised.
+- **Before the cutover:** delete the secret `PRIVATE_DATA_TOKEN`; every step goes back to a no-op.
+- **After the cutover:** Actions → Private data connection check → action `rollback`, confirm `ROLLBACK`. It puts every private file back into the public repository, removes the mode file and restarts the bot. **It publishes them again.**
